{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Hear, O Israel.</b> Contemplate and understand this." "<b>YHWH.</b> Who grants existence to every created being." "<b>Our Elohim.</b> He is the most choice of the separate intelligences relative to us, from whom we hope to attain our purposes without intermediary. And from the side of His being supreme in creative power, He alone is fit for prostration. And from the side that our hope is from Him without intermediary, it is fitting that to Him alone we pray and serve." "<b>YHWH is one.</b> Since He grants existence after absolute privation, it is established that nothing else exists of His kind of existence, and that He is distinct in kind from the existence of the world of corruptibles and from the existence of the world of the spheres and from the existence of the world of the angels, so that He is unique in His fourth world. This appears to be alluded to by the letter dalet of אחד being large, and by the letter ayin of שמע being large it is alluded to that it is fitting to open the eye and enlarge contemplation on this. Therefore the Sages said (Berakhot, chapter Heh Korei): provided one lengthens the dalet of אחד, in order to direct one's intention to this."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:20:43.821975855Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}